ISSPACE(3)                     P32W Unix                      ISSPACE(3)

NAME
       isspace, isxdigit, ispunct, isprint, isgraph, iscntrl - classify

SYNOPSIS
       #include <ctype.h>

       int isspace(int c);
       int isxdigit(int c);
       int ispunct(int c);
       int isprint(int c);
       int isgraph(int c);
       int iscntrl(int c);

DESCRIPTION
       Like the functions of ctype(3), each returns 1 if the
       character c is of its class in the ASCII table, else 0;
       values outside 0 to 127 belong to no class.

       isspace    white space: space, tab (\t), newline (\n),
                  vertical tab (\v), form feed (\f), return (\r)
       isxdigit   a hexadecimal digit: 0-9, a-f, A-F
       ispunct    printable, but not a space, letter or digit
       isprint    printable, the space included: 32 to 126
       isgraph    printable and not a space: 33 to 126
       iscntrl    a control character: 0 to 31, and DEL (127)

EXAMPLES
       for (p = line; *p; p++)
           if (!isprint(*p) && *p != '\t')
               *p = '?';

SEE ALSO
       ctype(3), toupper(3)

BUGS
       As for ctype(3): functions, not macros; ASCII only.
